<title>USA: Unions sue tobacco companies for health costs.</title>
<headline>Unions sue tobacco companies for health costs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four trade union health and welfare funds sued a group of tobacco companies and trade associations Monday to recoup funds spent on union members suffering from smoking related illnesses.</p>
<p>The suit was filed in New York State Supreme Court by the Eastern States Health &amp; Welfare Fund; ILGWU Health Services Plan; Health and Vacation Fund of the Amalgamated Ladies Garment Cutters Union Local 10 UNITE; and Health and Welfare Fund of Local 99 UNITE.</p>
<p>The suit also seeks to overcome provisions of the proposed $368.5 billion national settlement of tobacco litigation that could limit the amount of damages recovered.</p>
</text>
